WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.249 --> 00:00:18.711
doesn't seem very excited about the expedition," Zann said to Boz the next day.

2
00:00:19.431 --> 00:00:21.452
They were at Teplo's house, preparing to depart.

3
00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:24.154
"Why are her parents making her go?"

4
00:00:24.174 --> 00:00:29.116
"Her uncle Gar is an important member of the expedition," Boz said.

5
00:00:29.824 --> 00:00:34.367
"Gliss' parents thought this would be a good educational opportunity for her."

6
00:00:35.187 --> 00:00:36.087
Zann didn't believe it.

7
00:00:36.428 --> 00:00:39.749
He wondered if Gliss' parents were trying to push her and Zann together again.

8
00:00:39.769 --> 00:00:44.532
They probably weren't happy that she had become so close to Darb, a Void.

9
00:00:45.252 --> 00:00:48.514
Teplo rushed in, his goose snapping irritably at his heels.

10
00:00:49.274 --> 00:00:49.915
"Ready to go?"

11
00:00:50.315 --> 00:00:50.975
Teplo asked.

12
00:00:50.995 --> 00:00:54.977
"Ready." Boz grabbed Zann by the elbow and snapped his fingers.

13
00:00:55.758 --> 00:00:59.560
Zann barely had time to grab Zing before his grandfather zapped them away.

14
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.923
They landed on a grassy lawn, in front of an ancient stone mansion.

15
00:01:04.684 --> 00:01:06.365
Beyond was deep forest.

16
00:01:06.385 --> 00:01:08.367
"Where are we?"

17
00:01:08.787 --> 00:01:10.129
Zann spotted a large ship.

18
00:01:10.949 --> 00:01:14.432
A heap of colorful fabric was attached to it by a number of heavy ropes.

19
00:01:14.452 --> 00:01:16.474
"And what's that?"

20
00:01:17.255 --> 00:01:21.818
"This place is called Moonstone Manor," Teplo said, appearing beside them.

21
00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:25.702
"And that's the airship that will transport us to the Cave."

22
00:01:27.363 --> 00:01:28.264
Zann was surprised.

23
00:01:28.768 --> 00:01:35.031
"I know people can't just zap to the Cave of the Unknown because of its weird energy—" "Correct,"

24
00:01:35.371 --> 00:01:36.211
Teplo interrupted.

25
00:01:36.231 --> 00:01:42.774
"The Cave, as well as the relics inside, constantly sends out destabilizing surges.

26
00:01:43.735 --> 00:01:47.136
It makes performing any magic near the Cave very dangerous."

27
00:01:48.077 --> 00:01:51.558
"But I didn't know there was a special airship," Zann continued.

28
00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:55.100
"I assumed we'd fly there on dragons or something."

29
00:01:55.996 --> 00:02:00.397
"The Cave's unstable energy frightens most creatures," someone said.

30
00:02:01.438 --> 00:02:02.038
It was Venna.

31
00:02:02.598 --> 00:02:07.339
"Even the best-trained riding dragons usually refuse to fly anywhere near it."

32
00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:10.620
Venna was representing the Red Council on the expedition.

33
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.361
Beside her was a tall, handsome man.

34
00:02:14.201 --> 00:02:16.862
Venna introduced him as Tok, the airship's pilot.

35
00:02:17.642 --> 00:02:18.462
She turned to Zann.

36
00:02:18.482 --> 00:02:23.443
"This vehicle is the traditional way of traveling to the Cave of the Unknown," she said.

37
00:02:23.463 --> 00:02:25.584
"Come inside and have a look."

38
00:02:27.084 --> 00:02:29.565
The airship's main room looked like someone's living room.

39
00:02:30.325 --> 00:02:32.686
Tok led the way down a hallway and into another room.

40
00:02:33.406 --> 00:02:39.308
Three large, vicious-looking creatures with fiery red scales were writhing in a tank of thick glass.

41
00:02:40.048 --> 00:02:43.409
When Zann and the others entered, the creatures spit balls of flame at them.

42
00:02:44.249 --> 00:02:46.950
Zann jumped back, and Zing cowered behind him.

43
00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.570
But the flames didn't penetrate the glass wall.

44
00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.631
"Are those dragons?"

45
00:02:52.111 --> 00:02:52.651
Zann asked.

46
00:02:52.671 --> 00:02:54.612
"I've never seen any like that!"

47
00:02:55.764 --> 00:02:58.787
"They're known as flame furies," Teplo explained.

48
00:02:59.527 --> 00:03:01.689
"They originally came from another world."

49
00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:08.695
"And many years ago," said Boz, "several young furies were smuggled into Magica.

50
00:03:09.435 --> 00:03:14.359
They've been breeding in the darkest reaches of the forest beyond Mount Mystery ever since.

51
00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:16.901
Few people know they exist."

52
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:20.144
Venna nodded.

53
00:03:20.492 --> 00:03:26.075
"The original owner of this manor caught these three furies and found a way to harness their fiery

54
00:03:26.135 --> 00:03:27.756
power to travel to the Cave."

55
00:03:28.657 --> 00:03:30.117
She swept a hand at the vehicle.

56
00:03:30.137 --> 00:03:32.959
"He called it the Dragon Wagon."

57
00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:35.961
Zann stared at the fierce creatures.

58
00:03:36.521 --> 00:03:38.402
He wished Darb could be there to see them.

59
00:03:39.022 --> 00:03:41.343
Darb loved learning about new magical creatures!

60
00:03:41.363 --> 00:03:47.567
"When we're ready to go," Tok explained, "we'll release an image of the snuffer, which is the furies'

61
00:03:47.607 --> 00:03:50.756
natural enemy from their home world.

62
00:03:50.776 --> 00:03:54.278
The furies will blast it with their flaming breath until the image is removed."

63
00:03:55.218 --> 00:04:00.300
"Or until the image is so singed that the furies realize it's not real," Teplo said.

64
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.341
"Indeed." Tok chuckled.

65
00:04:03.361 --> 00:04:06.563
"We have to replace the fake snuffer for each journey."

66
00:04:07.323 --> 00:04:10.564
Zann wondered what kind of terrifying creature could scare the furies.

67
00:04:11.705 --> 00:04:15.626
Before he could ask, several other people entered, including Gliss and her uncle.

68
00:04:16.406 --> 00:04:19.868
Uncle Gar greeted everyone cheerfully, but Gliss looked glum.

69
00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.722
Zann could tell she wasn't thrilled to be there.

70
00:04:22.742 --> 00:04:25.383
"Let's get started," said Venna.

71
00:04:25.684 --> 00:04:27.225
"We have a long journey ahead."

72
00:04:28.025 --> 00:04:28.666
Tok nodded.

73
00:04:29.186 --> 00:04:30.006
"Snuffer up."

74
00:04:32.488 --> 00:04:35.350
A metal sculpture popped into view at the back of the furies' tank.

75
00:04:37.512 --> 00:04:39.113
"That's a snuffer?"

76
00:04:39.513 --> 00:04:40.173
Zann exclaimed.

77
00:04:40.193 --> 00:04:44.136
"There's one of those on my parents' storage shelf at the lab!"

78
00:04:44.156 --> 00:04:46.998
"That makes sense," Teplo said.

79
00:04:47.018 --> 00:04:49.600
"Their last journey was to the Cave.

80
00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.678
Well, second-to-last."

81
00:04:56.723 --> 00:04:58.064
The airship shuddered and lifted.

82
00:04:58.084 --> 00:05:01.427
"You should go sit down," Tok said to the group.

83
00:05:02.108 --> 00:05:05.552
"It can be tricky keeping your balance when the airship takes off."

84
00:05:06.453 --> 00:05:09.976
The furies' fiery breath quickly filled the Dragon Wagon's cloth balloon.

85
00:05:11.137 --> 00:05:13.440
Soon the airship was flying over the treetops.

86
00:05:17.632 --> 00:05:20.293
Zann spent the first hour of the journey peering out the window.

87
00:05:21.093 --> 00:05:23.254
Then Gliss' uncle called Zann's name.

88
00:05:23.274 --> 00:05:28.475
"You kids don't have to sit here with us boring old people," he said with a wink.

89
00:05:29.515 --> 00:05:32.436
"Why don't you two explore the rest of the ship together?"

90
00:05:33.256 --> 00:05:34.457
Zann forced a smile.

91
00:05:35.197 --> 00:05:38.238
He didn't want the adults to know that he and Gliss weren't on good terms.

92
00:05:38.258 --> 00:05:40.978
"Sure. Let's go, Gliss."

93
00:05:41.719 --> 00:05:44.099
They headed into the hallway leading to the furies' tank.

94
00:05:44.119 --> 00:05:46.100
"Are you still mad at me?"

95
00:05:46.484 --> 00:05:47.805
Gliss asked tentatively.

96
00:05:47.825 --> 00:05:51.869
"You know how important finding my parents is to me."

97
00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:53.491
He glared at her.

98
00:05:53.511 --> 00:05:55.372
"At least you should know."

99
00:05:55.392 --> 00:05:57.794
"Zann—" Gliss began.

100
00:05:58.255 --> 00:06:00.297
Zing interrupted her with an excited squawk.

101
00:06:00.897 --> 00:06:02.118
The little dragon rushed forward.

102
00:06:02.138 --> 00:06:05.361
"Zing, leave the furies alone," Zann said.

103
00:06:05.381 --> 00:06:07.423
"They'll roast you alive!"

104
00:06:08.164 --> 00:06:09.725
But Zing wasn't heading for the tank.

105
00:06:10.466 --> 00:06:12.308
He was scratching at a large feed bin.

106
00:06:13.248 --> 00:06:18.270
The expedition leaders had packed plenty of food for humans and dragons alike, since it was risky to

107
00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.650
conjure anything near the Cave.

108
00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.330
"Is he hungry?"

109
00:06:21.671 --> 00:06:22.231
Gliss wondered.

110
00:06:22.971 --> 00:06:24.211
Zann hurried over to the bin.

111
00:06:24.231 --> 00:06:27.652
"I guess Tok wouldn't mind if Zing had a snack."

112
00:06:28.393 --> 00:06:31.173
He swung open the top and gasped in shock.

113
00:06:31.914 --> 00:06:34.034
Perda and Darb were crouched inside!

114
00:06:34.054 --> 00:06:36.815
"Surprise!" Perda stood up.

115
00:06:36.835 --> 00:06:39.036
"We didn't want to miss all the fun!"
